## 5. Second Bug: Subscription Billing Unit Mismatch

In `/src/jobs/subscription_billing_job.cpp`:

```cpp
void SubscriptionBillingJob::execute_billing(const std::string& user_id, int monthly_fee_cents) {
    // BUG: Passing raw cents directly to a function expecting dollars.
    // It should perform: payment_.charge(user_id, monthly_fee_cents / 100.0, Currency::USD);
    payment_.charge(user_id, monthly_fee_cents, Currency::USD);
}
```

The parameter is named `monthly_fee_cents` (an integer count of cents), but it is passed as-is to `PaymentService::charge()`, which expects dollars. A fee of `1500` cents ($15.00) would charge `1500.0` dollars instead. Tested by `test_005.cpp`.

